WEBVTT

00:36.161 --> 00:38.955
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

00:50.633 --> 00:52.177
Hello, everyone!

00:52.260 --> 00:53.344
-Hello!
-Hello!

00:58.558 --> 00:59.851
We've got this!

01:02.520 --> 01:05.398
It's the end of the year!
Let's make some money!

01:11.780 --> 01:14.532
THE LOYAL CATERING

01:19.287 --> 01:20.455
All right!

01:20.538 --> 01:21.831
-You're good to go!
-Okay.

01:21.915 --> 01:23.041
-Drive safely!
-Will do!

01:49.984 --> 01:53.196
Have you ever asked for help before?

01:53.822 --> 01:55.573
I'm not talking about

01:56.199 --> 01:57.200
simply asking for help.

01:58.118 --> 01:59.410
I mean, when you're really struggling.

01:59.994 --> 02:01.287
Who'd do that?

02:01.871 --> 02:03.581
Make sure you ask me, okay?

02:15.176 --> 02:19.139
There's a worst kind of feeling
I never want to go through.

02:20.306 --> 02:21.182
It's hard

02:22.058 --> 02:23.560
to put into words.

02:24.310 --> 02:26.646
It's like being trapped in a hole

02:27.772 --> 02:32.318
that's only 30 cm wide but 100 m deep,
unable to move an inch.

02:32.402 --> 02:33.570
That's what it's like,

02:34.320 --> 02:36.990
but now that I know I can ask for help,

02:38.116 --> 02:40.743
that 30 cm hole

02:42.120 --> 02:45.790
feels about a meter wide now.

02:48.334 --> 02:49.419
So promise me

02:50.503 --> 02:53.798
that you'll ask for help, okay?

02:54.716 --> 02:55.758
Okay.

03:00.805 --> 03:03.474
To pull you out from self-destructing,

03:04.601 --> 03:07.186
I threw myself into that emotion…

03:09.939 --> 03:13.192
dove deep into it,
and found the words to save you.

03:14.694 --> 03:16.613
Words I've never spoken in my life.

03:18.197 --> 03:19.115
"Help me."

03:21.284 --> 03:23.703
But the words I found to save you

03:24.829 --> 03:26.205
ended up saving me instead.

03:32.587 --> 03:36.841
NO ONE COMES INTO YOUR LIFE BY MISTAKE

03:43.348 --> 03:45.850
When you get out of
a worst-case situation,

03:45.934 --> 03:48.561
it suddenly opens up a new perspective,

03:49.145 --> 03:52.857
and everything you struggled with before
starts to feel trivial.

03:53.983 --> 03:55.401
Success?

03:55.485 --> 03:56.694
Debuting?

03:57.320 --> 03:58.238
Screw all that.

03:59.364 --> 04:01.574
If I had just one wish in life,

04:02.784 --> 04:04.244
it would be to die of old age.

04:05.620 --> 04:08.122
I hope cats, trees,

04:08.206 --> 04:11.000
and all living things die of old age.

04:12.752 --> 04:14.212
Not from illness,

04:15.505 --> 04:16.923
not from agony.

04:18.591 --> 04:20.385
I hope everything dies of old age

04:21.511 --> 04:22.971
like leaves falling from a tree.

04:30.812 --> 04:31.729
MA JAE-YEONG

04:32.355 --> 04:33.815
I'll credit you on the screenplay.

04:34.774 --> 04:35.817
But under a pseudonym.

04:36.442 --> 04:37.902
I refuse to put your real name on it.

04:38.528 --> 04:39.612
That's the best I can do.

04:47.745 --> 04:49.497
Is it okay to use "Yeong-sil"

04:49.580 --> 04:51.207
as my pseudonym?

04:52.041 --> 04:54.460
I like the idea
of living an easygoing life.

04:55.920 --> 04:57.046
I'd be grateful.

04:57.672 --> 04:59.257
I'm sure Yeong-sil would be honored too.

05:00.800 --> 05:01.718
Thank you.

05:12.353 --> 05:13.604
Yeong-sil.

05:17.400 --> 05:18.484
What's that?

05:19.319 --> 05:20.278
My pseudonym.

05:20.820 --> 05:21.821
Yeong-sil.

05:26.117 --> 05:27.869
You know what I mean.

05:27.952 --> 05:29.787
It's like when a guy
who has nothing going for him,

05:29.871 --> 05:32.582
but once a woman says he does,
he starts to seem that way.

05:32.665 --> 05:34.751
You start to think,
"He must have something I'm not aware of."

05:35.918 --> 05:38.254
Now that you like Hwang Dong-man,
he seems impressive.

05:38.838 --> 05:39.839
-Really?
-Yeah.

05:41.215 --> 05:42.925
I'll have to tell him that.

05:45.845 --> 05:47.221
Wow, he's really fast.

05:47.305 --> 05:48.931
That's amazing.

05:53.853 --> 05:56.064
-He's so fast.
-Wow, look at this.

05:57.231 --> 05:58.232
I'll leave you to it.

05:59.275 --> 06:00.109
Wait, but…

06:02.653 --> 06:04.530
My brother
really went to Daegwallyeong this time.

06:16.876 --> 06:19.128
Eun-a, have you been waiting long?

06:19.796 --> 06:21.172
-I just got here.
-I see.

06:25.343 --> 06:26.719
TANGERINE
5,000 WON

06:26.803 --> 06:27.762
That looks good.

06:28.721 --> 06:30.765
A time of serenity is approaching,

06:30.848 --> 06:33.935
when you can curl up under a blanket,
eat tangerines, and read comic books.

06:34.519 --> 06:36.938
Why does winter feel more serene?

06:39.482 --> 06:41.234
Because it makes you
go looking for warmth?

06:41.943 --> 06:42.985
You're right.

06:44.487 --> 06:47.698
By the way, I think I can send you
my revised draft this week.

06:47.782 --> 06:50.660
The screenplay
is getting more interesting.

06:51.410 --> 06:52.662
I'm excited to read it.

06:52.745 --> 06:58.167
Now I see why directors are eager
for you to tear apart their screenplays.

06:58.251 --> 07:00.753
When you send screenplays
to other producers,

07:00.837 --> 07:04.924
they just go on about the story structure
and the ending,

07:05.007 --> 07:07.677
throwing around technical terms.

07:07.760 --> 07:09.220
But you're different.

07:09.804 --> 07:11.430
You know exactly where I'm stuck

07:11.514 --> 07:15.017
and where I need to focus emotionally
so I can really take off.

07:16.352 --> 07:17.562
You know,

07:18.146 --> 07:20.273
you have a real gift for reading people.

07:21.023 --> 07:22.358
I guess that's a skill

07:23.192 --> 07:24.318
you're just born with, right?

07:26.154 --> 07:27.613
Come on.

07:27.697 --> 07:29.907
You're the one who figured out
the "help me" emotion.

07:51.304 --> 07:52.180
May I ask why…

07:54.557 --> 07:56.726
that appeared on your watch?

08:01.147 --> 08:02.273
You don't have to answer.

08:07.278 --> 08:08.529
It was because of Jin-man.

08:18.956 --> 08:19.916
May I ask why

08:20.958 --> 08:22.877
that appeared on your watch?

08:26.130 --> 08:28.174
You don't have to answer me.

08:33.596 --> 08:34.597
It was because of my mom.

08:39.936 --> 08:41.229
Did you get along with your mom?

08:42.980 --> 08:43.940
We got along better

08:45.191 --> 08:46.400
after she passed away.

08:50.821 --> 08:53.115
I don't understand the phrase
"Look after your mom."

08:54.617 --> 08:57.495
My idea of a mom is so different
from everyone else's.

09:00.081 --> 09:01.749
Whenever I feel like I'm being abandoned,

09:02.792 --> 09:04.710
like my boyfriend leaving me

09:06.045 --> 09:07.630
or things going badly at work…

09:10.091 --> 09:12.301
my whole body aches, and I get nosebleeds.

09:13.678 --> 09:16.639
When I traced these symptoms
back to the source,

09:18.307 --> 09:20.017
they led to one person.

09:21.852 --> 09:23.813
The first person who wrote me off.

09:26.232 --> 09:27.066
My mom.

09:30.945 --> 09:32.530
I didn't know when I was young,

09:33.948 --> 09:35.908
but when I got older, I thought,

09:37.910 --> 09:39.829
"The woman who gave birth to me

09:41.080 --> 09:41.956
was such…

09:44.500 --> 09:45.960
a weak woman."

09:51.090 --> 09:52.592
That's when I decided

09:53.426 --> 09:56.012
that I'm going to become a strong mother
and a strong woman.

09:57.346 --> 09:59.015
Someone who wouldn't be ashamed

09:59.098 --> 10:01.726
of her child or her husband.

10:02.351 --> 10:04.395
A strong mother and a strong woman.

10:07.356 --> 10:08.357
That's a relief.

10:09.609 --> 10:10.735
You see,

10:10.818 --> 10:13.029
I'm a really embarrassing guy.

10:14.447 --> 10:15.865
I wouldn't say "really."

10:18.075 --> 10:19.201
Just a little.

10:22.663 --> 10:24.040
You're a little embarrassing

10:24.915 --> 10:27.793
but very lovable.

11:17.051 --> 11:18.677
The goddess of the wind!

11:36.112 --> 11:38.197
Who would dare abandon you?

11:38.989 --> 11:42.535
Who would dare write you off?

11:43.786 --> 11:44.870
Feel free to use me

11:45.579 --> 11:48.249
until I'm no longer needed.

11:49.708 --> 11:51.419
I'll be here waiting for you
if you return.

11:51.502 --> 11:53.421
The goddess of the wind!

11:53.504 --> 11:55.381
I'm a lifelong Byeon Eun-a admirer

11:56.006 --> 11:58.008
and someone you can come to anytime.

11:59.135 --> 12:00.052
It's the goddess of the wind!

12:00.136 --> 12:02.972
If it pains you to see me live like that,

12:03.722 --> 12:04.890
I'll meet another woman

12:05.599 --> 12:06.434
for a little while.

12:07.643 --> 12:09.228
Just for a moment.

12:10.229 --> 12:11.772
And if you tell me to come back,

12:11.856 --> 12:13.649
I'll run back to you.

12:14.358 --> 12:16.318
No, if I meet another woman,

12:17.778 --> 12:19.488
I'll say, "Byeon Eun-a controls me."

12:20.531 --> 12:23.325
"I must rush back to her
whenever she calls."

12:24.243 --> 12:25.911
This is what I'll say
before seeing someone.

12:26.829 --> 12:28.622
If you want me to remain single

12:29.832 --> 12:32.001
or be on standby forever,

12:32.084 --> 12:33.419
I'll do that.

12:34.503 --> 12:37.089
If that's enough to ease your anxiety,

12:38.507 --> 12:40.634
isn't that a wonderful way to live?

12:41.510 --> 12:43.804
Jeez, what am I going to do?

12:44.930 --> 12:46.765
I'm such a lovable bastard.

12:48.934 --> 12:49.894
Shouldn't you head up?

12:52.313 --> 12:53.856
Go upstairs already.

12:53.939 --> 12:55.191
The writer will be here soon.

12:55.274 --> 12:57.818
What's the point?
It's not happening anyway.

13:05.576 --> 13:06.660
Have you read their writing?

13:06.744 --> 13:08.204
I can't even look at it.

13:08.787 --> 13:11.040
There's a typo in the first line.
Are they insane?

13:11.123 --> 13:14.710
A real writer reviews their work
at least 20 times before submitting.

13:15.794 --> 13:16.962
Should I tell them not to come

13:17.588 --> 13:19.006
20 minutes before the appointment?

13:19.590 --> 13:21.050
Should I tell them to go back

13:21.133 --> 13:22.843
when they're coming
all the way from Dongducheon?

13:22.927 --> 13:25.930
I told you I'm not co-writing,
so why'd you set up an appointment?

13:26.013 --> 13:27.223
I warned you.

13:27.306 --> 13:28.807
You can't do it alone this time.

13:29.850 --> 13:31.060
Go upstairs.

13:31.143 --> 13:33.312
Go upstairs, interview the writer,

13:33.938 --> 13:36.232
and tear them apart
if that's what you want.

13:36.315 --> 13:41.070
But I'll search the whole country
to find you a co-writer.

13:42.655 --> 13:44.365
Just go upstairs.

13:45.324 --> 13:47.409
If an appointment was made,
you should show up.

13:54.083 --> 13:56.126
-You said to tear them apart!
-Go ahead!

13:57.336 --> 13:58.671
Man, that punk.

13:59.296 --> 14:00.756
Go easy on him.

14:01.340 --> 14:02.383
You know how he is.

14:03.384 --> 14:04.260
He's the type

14:05.094 --> 14:06.595
who needs constant praise

14:06.679 --> 14:09.807
to get his brain to kick in
and think clearly.

14:09.890 --> 14:10.766
What is he, a kid?

14:16.313 --> 14:19.316
Write something already
instead of sitting around all day.

14:19.900 --> 14:20.776
Hey, you…

14:24.697 --> 14:26.532
My brain's working.

14:27.116 --> 14:28.409
RESUME
NAME: PARK JEONG-MIN

14:28.492 --> 14:30.661
I thought you were a guy
because of your name.

14:30.744 --> 14:32.204
I get that a lot.

14:34.164 --> 14:37.042
They say female writers
hate male writers the most.

14:40.588 --> 14:42.548
We don't like female writers either

14:42.631 --> 14:45.509
because they're full of themselves
and stubborn as hell.

14:45.593 --> 14:48.220
That's how we see male writers too.

14:54.143 --> 14:56.145
-I see you've done a lot of co-writing.
-Yes.

14:56.228 --> 14:57.605
I haven't worked solo yet.

14:57.688 --> 14:58.564
Why?

14:59.732 --> 15:01.984
I'm not at that level yet.

15:02.067 --> 15:03.611
You've only been credited as a co-writer.

15:04.194 --> 15:06.196
-Yes.
-Did the lead writers find you helpful?

15:06.280 --> 15:08.532
Well, we're on good terms.

15:08.616 --> 15:10.200
You can be bad at your job
and still be on good terms

15:10.284 --> 15:12.369
if the lead writers
grit their teeth and bear it.

15:13.078 --> 15:14.204
I see.

15:15.748 --> 15:18.250
This is a bloody, intense screenplay.

15:18.334 --> 15:20.920
I'm not sure if a woman can handle it.

15:21.837 --> 15:22.922
You know what it's about?

15:23.005 --> 15:25.215
Yes, I heard from Producer Jung.

15:25.299 --> 15:28.218
The government takes out people
who stress out citizens.

15:28.302 --> 15:31.305
It's cathartic
and has the makings of a big hit.

15:31.388 --> 15:33.974
You think it'll be a big hit too, right?

15:34.058 --> 15:35.476
-Yes.
-You're right.

15:35.559 --> 15:38.354
Then tell me why I have to work with you.

15:40.314 --> 15:41.315
Excuse me?

15:41.398 --> 15:42.900
Let me be honest with you.

15:44.735 --> 15:47.279
If you work with me,
you won't get any credit.

15:47.363 --> 15:50.574
I'll say I did it all myself.

15:53.327 --> 15:54.870
All the good scenes,

15:54.954 --> 15:55.913
all the crappy scenes,

15:55.996 --> 15:58.832
and all the insults and praise
will be mine.

15:58.916 --> 16:00.334
I hate sharing with others.

16:00.417 --> 16:03.003
Anyone asking for "just one bite" is dead.

16:03.087 --> 16:06.423
The ones I despise most are the bastards
who ask for "just one bite."

16:06.507 --> 16:07.925
They won't get a single bite.

16:09.468 --> 16:10.803
Why are you laughing? I'm serious.

16:11.387 --> 16:12.262
If you do this,

16:12.930 --> 16:16.392
you can't tell a single soul
that you worked on it,

16:16.475 --> 16:18.435
and you can't do any interviews, period.

16:18.519 --> 16:20.229
I'm the only one who'll do interviews.

16:20.312 --> 16:22.314
Not even the actors
will do more interviews than me!

16:22.398 --> 16:23.524
It'll be a big hit,

16:24.566 --> 16:25.859
so all the credit is mine.

16:26.735 --> 16:29.279
I've taken all the criticism so far,
so why share the credit?

16:30.197 --> 16:33.909
I've still got four more writers
to meet after you,

16:33.993 --> 16:35.577
but I haven't read anything they sent.

16:35.661 --> 16:37.454
I don't read other people's writing.

16:38.122 --> 16:40.082
Why? Because it's boring.

16:40.165 --> 16:42.251
My writing is the most entertaining
in the world.

16:42.334 --> 16:44.503
Either way, I'm going to take full credit,

16:44.586 --> 16:46.672
and if I don't like your writing,
I'll fire you.

16:46.755 --> 16:50.300
It's fine as long as you don't go around
saying you wrote it.

16:50.384 --> 16:53.512
But you still have to work freaking hard.

16:54.471 --> 16:55.514
You still want the job?

16:58.392 --> 16:59.727
Why do you keep laughing? I'm serious.

16:59.810 --> 17:01.979
Are you confident
you can keep your mouth shut

17:02.062 --> 17:05.065
whenever this screenplay
comes up in conversation?

17:05.149 --> 17:09.069
The second you say you wrote this,
I'll go ballistic and curse you out.

17:09.820 --> 17:10.779
Are you up for it?

17:12.990 --> 17:14.033
Director Park.

17:16.243 --> 17:18.078
You're hilarious.

17:19.538 --> 17:21.874
You're the funniest director
I've ever met.

17:51.361 --> 17:52.362
I didn't order that.

17:54.990 --> 17:56.617
Why are you standing there frozen?

17:56.700 --> 17:57.534
Unfreeze!

18:08.045 --> 18:11.757
Director Park, you're hilarious.

18:11.840 --> 18:14.384
You're the funniest director
I've ever met.

18:22.017 --> 18:23.018
Oh jeez.

18:26.647 --> 18:29.316
Please knock before you come out.

18:32.986 --> 18:34.446
What were you looking at?

18:34.530 --> 18:35.531
Nothing, ma'am.

18:35.614 --> 18:36.448
It's a joke.

18:36.532 --> 18:38.075
Just kidding.

18:43.455 --> 18:44.873
Tomorrow's interview is at 4 p.m.

18:49.294 --> 18:50.420
I said it's at 4 p.m.

18:51.046 --> 18:52.756
Why bother?
I'll go with the one I saw today.

18:56.218 --> 18:57.678
We just have to work together, no?

18:57.761 --> 18:59.888
But it should be a writer
who can actually help.

18:59.972 --> 19:01.140
She did help.

19:02.307 --> 19:03.225
Look, it doesn't matter.

19:03.308 --> 19:05.435
I'm writing it alone anyway,
so let's just go with her.

19:05.519 --> 19:07.187
You said the first line had a typo.

19:08.063 --> 19:10.232
-What kind of writer does that?
-Are we writing a book?

19:10.858 --> 19:12.192
Are we publishing it?

19:12.860 --> 19:14.403
Who cares about typos?

19:16.864 --> 19:17.990
We just need ideas.

19:18.574 --> 19:19.449
Does she have ideas?

19:20.117 --> 19:21.118
I'm sure she does.

19:28.458 --> 19:29.793
I said I'll work with her.

19:31.753 --> 19:33.046
Isn't that enough?

19:35.257 --> 19:37.968
You're the funniest director
I've ever met.

19:50.439 --> 19:52.191
-Hey, what's up?
-Where are you?

19:52.774 --> 19:54.318
I came out for a bit. Why?

19:56.111 --> 19:57.696
I wanted to ask you what Eun-a's up to.

19:57.779 --> 19:59.323
What for?

19:59.406 --> 20:01.491
I sent her my revised draft about…

20:02.951 --> 20:04.328
nine and a half hours ago.

20:05.078 --> 20:05.913
But there's no word.

20:06.788 --> 20:07.623
Are you scared?

20:08.749 --> 20:11.835
I pulled an all-nighter,
so I should be sleeping, but I can't.

20:13.170 --> 20:15.380
I sent it, but looking at it again,
it's not great.

20:16.381 --> 20:20.802
Hey, if Mr. Choi catches her reading it
during work hours, she'll get chewed out.

20:20.886 --> 20:22.930
She'll probably get back to you tonight,
so just stay scared until then.

20:23.013 --> 20:24.556
Oh jeez.

20:25.140 --> 20:28.393
Please, please, please be a good read.

20:28.477 --> 20:30.562
Please be a good read.

20:30.646 --> 20:32.356
This is Writer Park Jeong-min.

20:32.439 --> 20:33.523
She's a woman.

20:33.607 --> 20:35.442
This is Team Leader Lee In-yeong
from the streaming company.

20:35.525 --> 20:38.028
-Right.
-Hello, nice to meet you.

20:39.655 --> 20:40.614
Thank you.

20:42.616 --> 20:45.202
I'm so relieved
you found a writer so quickly.

20:45.285 --> 20:49.081
We worried it might've been impolite
to suggest a co-writer to you.

20:49.164 --> 20:50.832
Oh, it wasn't impolite.

20:50.916 --> 20:51.959
It was rude.

20:56.672 --> 20:58.840
We just want to produce good work quickly.

20:59.633 --> 21:01.718
Did you hear that?
We have to write quickly.

21:02.386 --> 21:05.347
Jeez, we're not a factory
that can churn out writing quickly.

21:07.432 --> 21:09.559
I hear this is your first time co-writing.

21:09.643 --> 21:11.186
I hope you two work well together.

21:11.270 --> 21:13.105
I think co-writing is great.

21:13.188 --> 21:15.023
I'm going to keep doing it from now on.

21:15.607 --> 21:19.069
I spend more time playing games
than I do writing.

21:19.653 --> 21:20.988
But I have to be careful.

21:21.071 --> 21:22.739
"Should I play a round or not?"

21:22.823 --> 21:26.285
There's pressure to always look
fully absorbed in your work.

21:26.868 --> 21:28.578
You didn't play a single round today.

21:28.662 --> 21:29.705
But I did.

21:29.788 --> 21:31.915
I played a round in the bathroom.

21:35.168 --> 21:36.837
Hey, I'm heading out first.

21:37.421 --> 21:38.255
See you tomorrow.

21:39.506 --> 21:40.549
-We're leaving now.
-Goodbye.

22:00.110 --> 22:02.821
WEATHER MAKER
BY HWANG DONG-MAN

22:05.991 --> 22:07.284
I'll read it carefully.

22:20.422 --> 22:22.883
Let's not do this in our next life.

22:22.966 --> 22:24.509
It isn't worth doing.

22:25.594 --> 22:26.970
After working your ass off writing,

22:27.888 --> 22:30.807
you're on pins and needles,
like a kid waiting to be punished.

22:30.891 --> 22:33.393
Back in the day, it wasn't so agonizing

22:33.477 --> 22:34.936
for people in the arts.

22:35.020 --> 22:37.355
They just lived the way they were born.

22:37.439 --> 22:38.648
Geniuses?

22:38.732 --> 22:40.734
They're not geniuses for being impressive.

22:40.817 --> 22:41.985
They were just born that way.

22:42.611 --> 22:46.740
It wasn't about
someone being gifted at this or that.

22:46.823 --> 22:50.202
Everyone just lived naturally,
the way they were born.

22:50.952 --> 22:54.122
I've got no talent, but some strange urge
led me to this line of work,

22:54.206 --> 22:55.999
and now I'm going through hell.

22:56.583 --> 22:57.918
We should leave art

22:58.001 --> 23:00.045
for the geniuses to do.

23:01.046 --> 23:02.631
And leave studying for smart people.

23:03.965 --> 23:06.093
I'd be writing my ass off
instead of sitting around.

23:06.176 --> 23:09.513
Hey, what am I supposed to write
when I've got nothing?

23:09.596 --> 23:11.181
Should I string together the alphabet?

23:14.226 --> 23:16.603
Hey, why don't you give us
something like this too?

23:16.686 --> 23:17.813
Instead of this crap!

23:19.064 --> 23:21.191
Look at you, bringing out the fancy stuff
for your special guest.

23:26.113 --> 23:27.447
Who's here?

23:27.531 --> 23:28.532
Oh Jeong-hui.

23:28.615 --> 23:29.741
What? Oh Jeong-hui?

23:43.964 --> 23:45.799
She was probably terrified

23:45.882 --> 23:47.551
that her biological daughter
might turn up.

23:48.135 --> 23:49.678
Rumor has it she doesn't see her at all.

23:50.679 --> 23:54.558
We don't know
whether she doesn't or she can't.

23:55.851 --> 23:57.394
Have you worked with Oh Jeong-hui?

23:58.395 --> 23:59.688
-I have.
-Right.

23:59.771 --> 24:02.607
-One month?
-One month is enough to read someone.

24:02.691 --> 24:04.442
Even one day is enough.

24:04.526 --> 24:06.987
When I was a PA on the directing team
for Dogs and Cats,

24:07.070 --> 24:09.322
we used to drink vending machine coffee.

24:09.406 --> 24:12.284
Whenever I heard coins jingle,
I'd stand up right away.

24:12.909 --> 24:15.287
Why? Because getting coffee
was the PA's job.

24:15.370 --> 24:18.915
The second I heard coins jingle,
I'd jump up like Pavlov's dog.

24:18.999 --> 24:20.333
That day,

24:20.417 --> 24:23.461
I heard coins jingle and jumped up.

24:24.212 --> 24:25.547
Then I saw Oh Jeong-hui

24:26.965 --> 24:29.843
counting out coins in her hand

24:30.635 --> 24:32.637
as she walked out.

24:34.181 --> 24:36.725
She actually went out
and got her own coffee.

24:36.808 --> 24:37.726
I fell for her right then.

24:39.978 --> 24:42.147
That's the sort of thing
a PA on set falls for.

24:42.856 --> 24:44.191
I thought,

24:44.274 --> 24:47.736
"When I get older,
I'll take care of my own needs too."

24:48.403 --> 24:50.530
"I'll never have someone else to do it."

24:51.239 --> 24:52.699
You know why she does that?

24:54.910 --> 24:55.744
She enjoys it.

24:55.827 --> 24:57.537
The attention, that is.

24:57.621 --> 24:59.414
"Hey, it's Oh Jeong-hui!"

24:59.497 --> 25:01.833
That's why she goes everywhere herself.

25:01.917 --> 25:04.419
Pharmacy, grocery store, you name it.

25:04.502 --> 25:07.923
That's just your cynical way
of seeing things.

25:09.216 --> 25:12.552
If I hadn't quit like that back then…

25:14.971 --> 25:18.433
I'd at least be able to
exchange greetings with her by now.

25:25.065 --> 25:26.316
Hello.

25:26.399 --> 25:27.734
Oh, that's okay.

25:44.626 --> 25:46.044
WEATHER MAKER
BY HWANG DONG-MAN

26:15.407 --> 26:16.491
Hello.

26:17.409 --> 26:19.202
I emailed it to you already.

26:19.286 --> 26:20.412
You didn't receive it?

26:22.372 --> 26:24.207
I'm actually in a meeting right now.

26:25.292 --> 26:27.627
I'll have that ready
by the end of the year.

26:43.184 --> 26:46.146
They said the fifth revision
will be ready for you to review

26:46.229 --> 26:49.024
by the end of next month.

26:54.070 --> 26:55.155
Hello.

26:55.238 --> 26:57.365
I'm not sure if you remember me,

26:57.449 --> 27:00.452
but my name is Hwang Dong-man,
and I worked on the directing team

27:01.161 --> 27:02.579
for Dogs and Cats.

27:03.079 --> 27:04.080
Is that so?

27:04.664 --> 27:06.583
I'm sorry,
but I don't remember you at all.

27:06.666 --> 27:07.500
Right.

27:08.043 --> 27:09.085
I'm not surprised.

27:29.147 --> 27:30.815
The bastard went inside the room!

27:30.899 --> 27:32.108
What room?

27:32.192 --> 27:33.693
The one Oh Jeong-hui is in!

27:35.779 --> 27:37.447
Go drag him out of there right now!

27:38.406 --> 27:39.282
Hurry!

27:41.701 --> 27:43.787
-Oh, whatever. That crazy bastard.
-Hey!

27:48.917 --> 27:51.961
You probably don't remember me
because I quit after a month,

27:52.045 --> 27:54.339
but what I regretted most about quitting

27:54.422 --> 27:56.966
was not getting to watch your acting.

27:58.843 --> 28:00.678
The way you could
instantly raise the intensity,

28:00.762 --> 28:03.848
throw yourself into the role,
and slip into character.

28:03.932 --> 28:07.852
I watched from the set,
holding my breath and sweating.

28:08.770 --> 28:13.149
I couldn't even breathe
because I thought it might distract you.

28:13.650 --> 28:15.443
As soon as the director said, "Cut!"

28:15.527 --> 28:17.529
and you finally let out your breath,

28:17.612 --> 28:19.531
I found myself doing the same.

28:19.614 --> 28:24.202
I had a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity
to watch a legendary actor perform,

28:25.078 --> 28:26.830
and it led to a moment of enlightenment.

28:27.497 --> 28:32.335
I had only understood
film and acting in theory,

28:32.419 --> 28:36.131
but you made it clear what they truly are,
right in front of my eyes.

28:36.756 --> 28:37.799
And that feeling

28:39.384 --> 28:40.635
has stayed with me ever since.

28:42.095 --> 28:43.054
Thank you.

28:43.138 --> 28:45.181
You once looked at a screenplay and said,

28:46.599 --> 28:48.351
"The writing doesn't close in on me."

28:48.435 --> 28:49.269
"Close in."

28:50.395 --> 28:53.690
Hearing you say a phrase I've only heard
in the context of close-quarters combat

28:53.773 --> 28:55.024
really opened my eyes.

28:55.108 --> 28:59.612
"Close in" could only come from someone
who acts with their whole body.

29:00.238 --> 29:01.156
Even now,

29:02.449 --> 29:05.368
I ask myself,
"Is my writing closing in on me?"

29:05.452 --> 29:07.954
"Or am I just sitting here
overthinking it?"

29:08.997 --> 29:10.707
That became
a major guiding principle for me,

29:11.875 --> 29:13.501
and I always measure myself against it.

29:14.085 --> 29:15.962
I haven't heard that in a while.

29:16.045 --> 29:16.963
"Close in."

29:18.298 --> 29:19.966
I said it often back in the day.

29:20.049 --> 29:20.884
Yes.

29:22.302 --> 29:24.053
Though it was just a month,

29:24.137 --> 29:27.223
I learned so much
from simply observing you from a distance.

29:27.807 --> 29:29.893
So I really wanted to tell you

29:29.976 --> 29:33.104
that someone you don't even remember

29:33.688 --> 29:35.648
has been living by the words you once said

29:35.732 --> 29:39.110
as if they were
a guiding principle in his life.

29:40.528 --> 29:43.031
I really wanted to say that.

29:44.491 --> 29:45.408
Thank you.

29:46.618 --> 29:47.535
Thank you.

29:48.286 --> 29:49.579
What films have you done?

29:50.288 --> 29:51.498
I suddenly want to watch them.

29:58.922 --> 30:00.548
I haven't…

30:02.342 --> 30:04.385
I haven't been able to debut yet.

30:15.522 --> 30:17.732
Well, I'm sure you will soon.

30:19.359 --> 30:21.903
By the way, why did you quit back then?

30:22.987 --> 30:24.656
Did you get a better job offer?

30:29.869 --> 30:31.830
Do you remember…

30:33.790 --> 30:36.000
when we stopped filming for a few days…

30:39.462 --> 30:40.421
to remove an odor?

30:43.633 --> 30:45.385
Yes, that's right.

30:45.969 --> 30:48.888
I really had to relieve myself,

30:49.764 --> 30:52.267
so I had no choice
but to use the bathroom on set.

30:52.350 --> 30:54.644
Unfortunately, the toilet in the bathroom

30:54.727 --> 30:57.313
was merely a prop
placed directly on the floor.

30:57.897 --> 30:59.023
I had no idea

30:59.816 --> 31:00.942
because I was a newbie.

31:01.526 --> 31:03.611
I considered picking it up
and running with it,

31:03.695 --> 31:05.321
but it was open at the bottom,

31:06.364 --> 31:07.574
so I couldn't.

31:08.283 --> 31:12.412
I was in my twenties and very shy,
so I had no choice but to run away.

31:12.996 --> 31:16.124
Despite knowing the cliché
that the missing person is the culprit,

31:16.207 --> 31:18.084
I had no choice but to run.

31:18.918 --> 31:20.837
I sometimes think my debut

31:22.213 --> 31:23.423
would've come much sooner

31:24.674 --> 31:27.427
if I hadn't made that mistake.

31:32.682 --> 31:34.392
As your biggest fan,

31:35.018 --> 31:37.896
I'm putting aside my embarrassment

31:37.979 --> 31:38.980
to make this confession

31:39.772 --> 31:42.233
and to make a fresh start.

31:44.068 --> 31:44.903
Also,

31:45.528 --> 31:47.196
I sincerely congratulate you

31:47.906 --> 31:49.073
on your comeback

31:49.908 --> 31:50.742
after your setback.

32:03.838 --> 32:04.672
Now,

32:05.465 --> 32:07.425
if you'll excuse me.

32:20.063 --> 32:21.940
What the heck? Why are you here?

32:22.023 --> 32:23.274
I thought you were banned.

32:24.108 --> 32:25.610
The ban's been lifted.

32:32.700 --> 32:33.534
Lifted?

32:35.578 --> 32:36.412
What did he say?

32:36.996 --> 32:38.456
Just that he's a fan.

32:40.166 --> 32:41.834
That crazy bastard.

32:41.918 --> 32:44.337
There are always guys like him, you know.

32:44.420 --> 32:48.466
People who stay on the sidelines
but act as if they belong.

32:48.549 --> 32:52.136
He still hasn't debuted after 20 years
and is just hanging around.

32:52.887 --> 32:55.264
Darn, it was nice not seeing him around.

33:33.094 --> 33:34.178
Welcome.

33:41.144 --> 33:41.978
Let's go.

34:06.711 --> 34:09.422
Don't let anyone find out
that the poor kid Oh Jeong-hui abandoned

34:10.506 --> 34:12.050
is actually me.

34:13.593 --> 34:15.136
I won't let anyone find out either.

34:54.008 --> 34:54.926
Here.

34:55.802 --> 34:58.012
I'd like to ask for your help
with casting.

35:01.099 --> 35:02.183
Casting?

35:02.266 --> 35:03.101
Yes.

35:05.770 --> 35:07.563
"Knock knock knock"?

35:07.647 --> 35:09.315
What kind of title is this?

35:10.149 --> 35:12.151
The title must grab the actor's attention.

35:12.819 --> 35:14.487
The screenplay is good.

35:14.570 --> 35:15.863
It's well put together.

35:16.781 --> 35:19.909
It's by Director Ma Jae-yeong,
who won the production funding grant.

35:19.992 --> 35:22.703
His top choice is actor Noh Kang-sik.

35:23.788 --> 35:25.748
He's greedy for a newbie, isn't he?

35:25.832 --> 35:27.375
We're doing this on a government grant,

35:27.458 --> 35:29.961
so we can't work
with a big company like Choi Film,

35:30.044 --> 35:32.713
but if you help us,
I promise I'll make it up to you.

35:33.548 --> 35:35.299
I'm counting on you to put in a good word.

35:35.383 --> 35:36.926
Move on from projects like this.

35:37.009 --> 35:39.428
How long are you going to keep doing
government-funded projects?

35:40.012 --> 35:41.347
You have 20 years of experience.

35:41.430 --> 35:43.474
Do you really want to
live off government money?

35:44.058 --> 35:45.434
Yes, well,

35:45.518 --> 35:47.019
I have to make a living somehow.

35:47.103 --> 35:49.480
That's why you need to do
what makes money,

35:50.064 --> 35:51.816
not what's good.

35:51.899 --> 35:54.819
They say amateurs go for what's good,

35:54.902 --> 35:57.822
and pros go for what makes money.

35:57.905 --> 36:00.074
Isn't it time for you to turn pro, Ms. Ko?

36:00.158 --> 36:01.784
Come on, Pro Ko.

36:03.870 --> 36:07.582
Filmmakers act like starving
is some kind of badge of honor.

36:08.749 --> 36:10.251
I'll pass this on,

36:10.334 --> 36:11.627
but this is the last time.

36:12.211 --> 36:13.963
Do what makes money, all right?

36:18.384 --> 36:20.887
Why is Hwang Dong-man coming here again?

36:20.970 --> 36:22.305
He's come to his senses.

36:23.264 --> 36:24.599
I'll believe it when pigs fly.

36:26.142 --> 36:28.477
Nothing you do meets my approval.

36:31.939 --> 36:33.983
-You're leaving?
-I'm heading out.

36:34.066 --> 36:35.735
-Goodbye, sir.
-See you.

36:36.611 --> 36:37.445
See you.

36:42.909 --> 36:44.285
Jeez, it's pouring.

36:44.911 --> 36:45.828
Take it with you.

36:46.829 --> 36:48.080
Okay, thanks.

36:53.502 --> 36:54.503
Get home safely.

37:09.852 --> 37:10.853
You know…

37:13.314 --> 37:16.901
I can tolerate a guy sleeping around,
but not acting superior.

37:18.361 --> 37:20.613
And this guy keeps acting superior.

37:21.197 --> 37:22.240
Who do you mean?

37:24.200 --> 37:25.243
I'm heading home.

37:25.952 --> 37:27.245
-Take it easy.
-Yes, ma'am.

37:27.328 --> 37:28.621
I'm off.

37:28.704 --> 37:29.538
-See you.
-Okay.

37:49.308 --> 37:52.603
Is it that serious?

37:55.523 --> 37:57.984
It's okay. Please speak freely.

37:58.651 --> 38:00.152
I'll accept anything you say.

38:03.114 --> 38:04.865
I'll brace myself and make sure

38:04.949 --> 38:08.035
my face doesn't go blank
while listening to you.

38:08.786 --> 38:09.912
Ready.

38:09.996 --> 38:10.830
Action!

38:13.791 --> 38:15.501
Why are you so drunk?

38:16.294 --> 38:17.253
Because I'm scared.

38:18.963 --> 38:21.048
Why? It was great.

38:27.388 --> 38:28.514
I cried

38:29.140 --> 38:30.182
while reading it.

38:33.686 --> 38:35.313
I came running to give you a hug.

38:38.316 --> 38:39.608
So why are you scared?

38:40.860 --> 38:42.111
Oh gosh, I thought…

38:43.487 --> 38:45.823
Are you serious?

38:45.906 --> 38:48.868
The day's over, so let's drink!

38:49.827 --> 38:53.122
Make way! Jang Mi-ran is coming through!

38:53.205 --> 38:54.999
-So where are we…
-What?

38:55.875 --> 38:57.209
Hwang Dong-man!

38:57.293 --> 38:58.794
-Director Hwang!
-Mi-ran!

39:00.129 --> 39:01.547
-How have you been?
-I've been great.

39:02.340 --> 39:03.924
-Well, I…
-Enjoy your time.

39:04.008 --> 39:05.468
-Shall we…
-Oh my.

39:05.551 --> 39:06.927
-Hello, Mi-ran.
-Hello, Director Lee.

39:07.011 --> 39:08.179
-Gosh, you don't have to.
-Sorry?

39:11.307 --> 39:13.768
-Mi-ran!
-Oh, you too, Director Park?

39:18.314 --> 39:20.983
Why? What is it, Director Park?

39:21.067 --> 39:24.945
-My dear director!
-My dear actor!

39:25.029 --> 39:26.572
All right, let's drink!

39:26.655 --> 39:28.240
-Let's drink!
-Let's drink!

39:31.243 --> 39:32.995
Here comes the wave!

39:39.835 --> 39:40.753
Hey!

39:41.545 --> 39:42.963
Fill your glass! One more time!

39:43.047 --> 39:46.092
-Sounds good!
-Come on, one more shot!

39:46.675 --> 39:48.469
-Let's go!
-The wave started!

39:48.552 --> 39:50.596
Here it comes!

39:51.180 --> 39:53.265
Hey, that's not fair!

39:53.349 --> 39:54.809
Mi-ran, why aren't you drinking?

39:54.892 --> 39:56.852
You have to drink!

39:58.062 --> 39:59.355
Why aren't you drinking?

39:59.438 --> 40:01.440
If a scene looks well-written to me too,

40:01.524 --> 40:04.527
I go really hard on everyone
and do multiple takes.

40:05.569 --> 40:07.655
But if a scene looks bad to me,

40:07.738 --> 40:08.572
I shoot it quickly.

40:09.281 --> 40:10.699
I just rush through it

40:10.783 --> 40:12.493
before anyone catches on
that it's not good.

40:12.576 --> 40:13.744
Ready.

40:14.662 --> 40:15.955
Action, cut, okay!

40:16.038 --> 40:18.416
Cut, okay! Cut, okay!

40:18.499 --> 40:20.501
Cut, okay! Cut, okay! Cut, okay!

40:20.584 --> 40:21.836
My goodness.

40:21.919 --> 40:23.170
By the way,

40:23.254 --> 40:25.172
did you know

40:25.256 --> 40:26.799
there's a Dong-man in every class?

40:26.882 --> 40:28.509
The Dong-man
of the freshman class of 2008,

40:28.592 --> 40:29.885
the Dong-man
of the freshman class of 2009.

40:31.011 --> 40:35.724
They call the most problematic student
in that class year "Dong-man,"

40:35.808 --> 40:38.853
and there's always one every single year.

40:40.688 --> 40:43.232
There are Dong-mans in kindergarten too.

40:43.315 --> 40:46.986
They argue about who's closer to whom.

40:47.069 --> 40:51.782
They're all fighting hard
against their worthlessness too.

40:52.283 --> 40:54.577
-No regrets!
-What did I know?

40:54.660 --> 40:55.953
So I went searching for it.

40:56.036 --> 40:59.790
I searched and searched,
and even checked an English style guide.

41:00.374 --> 41:03.752
I'll never forget the first sentence
on the first page.

41:04.628 --> 41:08.174
"If you're not writing about sex,

41:09.633 --> 41:10.801
it'd better be really good."

41:13.012 --> 41:14.889
-Come on, how do you beat sex?
-How…

41:14.972 --> 41:18.100
Exactly. How do you beat that?

41:18.184 --> 41:19.018
You can't.

41:20.269 --> 41:21.479
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

41:23.689 --> 41:28.027
I wonder what it feels like
to call Ms. Oh Jeong-hui your mom.

41:33.115 --> 41:34.450
Shit?

41:34.533 --> 41:35.743
Shit.

41:35.826 --> 41:37.828
She thinks she'll go down in history.

41:37.912 --> 41:39.663
Wouldn't she, though?

41:39.747 --> 41:41.081
No, she won't.

41:41.165 --> 41:43.501
Everyone thinks
going down in history is easy,

41:43.584 --> 41:45.961
but no one ever does,
no matter how hard they try.

41:55.679 --> 41:58.807
Wherever I go,
I need to stand out the most.

42:00.351 --> 42:01.936
But you get on my nerves.

42:02.019 --> 42:03.395
You know you're pretty, right?

42:04.104 --> 42:05.481
So why do you dress carelessly?

42:06.065 --> 42:07.149
Are you dressed properly?

42:07.900 --> 42:08.776
No, you're not.

42:13.614 --> 42:15.324
When I was in elementary school,

42:15.908 --> 42:18.285
school life grew more difficult,

42:18.369 --> 42:20.871
so I deliberately
left my pencil case at home.

42:21.622 --> 42:22.790
And every day,

42:23.541 --> 42:26.001
I asked if I could borrow a pencil.

42:27.002 --> 42:29.672
I didn't know why I did that at the time,

42:31.423 --> 42:33.092
but I found out when I got older.

42:34.552 --> 42:36.595
I was trying to reduce my problem

42:37.388 --> 42:39.890
to just being the annoying kid
who borrowed pencils…

42:42.101 --> 42:44.144
because I was afraid
they'd find out my real problem.

42:47.648 --> 42:48.899
So that's why

42:50.067 --> 42:51.360
I dress carelessly.

42:54.363 --> 42:57.449
Is that the same as me speaking bluntly?

43:00.744 --> 43:02.496
You know you've got a weird talent, right?

43:03.622 --> 43:04.748
You have this ability

43:05.332 --> 43:06.875
to bring people back down to earth.

43:07.960 --> 43:09.461
I'm always floating around

43:09.545 --> 43:12.381
and going all over the place when I talk,

43:12.965 --> 43:14.091
but when I'm with you,

43:14.592 --> 43:16.385
I gracefully…

43:19.179 --> 43:20.514
come back down to earth.

43:29.148 --> 43:30.441
I won't let it happen today, though.

43:31.859 --> 43:33.360
Let's go for round two!

43:33.444 --> 43:36.155
-No! No more soju!
-Let's go!

43:36.238 --> 43:38.282
-Let's go for round two!
-Round two!

43:38.365 --> 43:41.243
I can't… I can't go to karaoke.

43:41.327 --> 43:42.286
Are you going?

43:42.870 --> 43:44.538
No karaoke, right?

43:44.622 --> 43:47.082
-No singing.
-No one's going home tonight!

43:47.166 --> 43:49.293
-She said no one's going home tonight!
-No one!

43:49.376 --> 43:50.919
-We're going to drink more!
-Come on!

43:51.003 --> 43:52.379
Ms. Lee!

43:52.463 --> 43:54.882
Ms. Lee, it's this way!

43:54.965 --> 43:57.343
Oh, I don't drink,

43:57.426 --> 43:59.011
so I'll take my car and meet you there.

43:59.803 --> 44:02.097
Hey, that woman's getting away.

44:02.681 --> 44:03.766
Let's take her car!

44:03.849 --> 44:05.809
-Let's take her car!
-Let's go!

44:05.893 --> 44:07.436
-Let's go!
-Where are we going?

44:07.519 --> 44:08.562
Come on, let's go!

44:08.646 --> 44:09.605
Yeong-su!

44:11.649 --> 44:13.359
Can I come in?

44:13.442 --> 44:15.361
-Can I come in?
-Why, of course!

44:15.444 --> 44:17.488
-Can I come in?
-Please go in!

44:18.238 --> 44:19.573
Come on!

44:19.657 --> 44:22.701
-Let's go!
-Yeong-su's trying to slip out!

44:22.785 --> 44:26.121
-It's 150,000 won for a set menu.
-We're definitely having squid.

44:26.205 --> 44:28.540
Ma'am! Two large squid platters, please!

44:28.624 --> 44:30.125
You can't have squid.

44:30.209 --> 44:32.878
-Just have rockfish.
-But I see them over there!

44:32.961 --> 44:34.046
They're too expensive.

44:34.129 --> 44:36.131
I put a few in there to lure customers.

44:36.215 --> 44:38.175
How expensive can it be? It's just squid!

44:38.258 --> 44:39.677
Two large squid platters!

44:39.760 --> 44:42.096
One squid costs 30,000 won.

44:42.179 --> 44:45.933
Then give us the rockfish, please!

44:52.690 --> 44:56.443
Hey, the customers are leaving.
Let's quiet down!

44:56.527 --> 44:58.987
You quiet down first!

45:00.572 --> 45:01.907
You're so loud.

45:04.243 --> 45:08.664
This is the first time I've ever woken up
excited to go to a meeting.

45:09.415 --> 45:14.294
The thought of meetings used to feel like
a heavy weight on my heart.

45:16.463 --> 45:19.216
I never knew work could be so much fun.

45:19.299 --> 45:20.634
-Where's the squid?
-Don't do that.

45:22.970 --> 45:24.888
Have you had enough to drink?

45:29.184 --> 45:32.354
I like all old movies.

45:33.647 --> 45:35.524
Movies nowadays are the most boring.

45:36.358 --> 45:40.237
With old films,
even the ones labeled as flops

45:40.320 --> 45:42.781
are pretty decent
once you start watching them.

45:42.865 --> 45:43.991
-Right.
-Yeah.

45:44.074 --> 45:46.493
Maybe I'm just nostalgic for the past,

45:47.703 --> 45:50.247
but it makes me feel good
when I see signs for tailor shops

45:51.081 --> 45:53.792
and electronics repair shops in movies.

45:58.589 --> 46:00.090
Do you want to hear an interesting story?

46:03.385 --> 46:04.678
It feels like

46:05.846 --> 46:06.972
we're here in the moment, right?

46:08.765 --> 46:09.808
But actually,

46:10.726 --> 46:12.144
we're just reminiscing.

46:13.979 --> 46:16.398
-Our lives have already ended.
-Okay.

46:16.482 --> 46:18.275
We're 99 years old,

46:18.358 --> 46:19.526
lying in bed,

46:20.402 --> 46:21.904
reliving the times we miss

46:22.946 --> 46:24.698
just before we die.

46:31.038 --> 46:32.998
What we're seeing right now

46:34.541 --> 46:35.959
is a scene from our memories

46:37.085 --> 46:39.087
that we relive just before we die.

46:53.435 --> 46:54.478
I think I get it.

46:59.024 --> 47:01.735
So right now…

47:04.112 --> 47:07.241
is this my memory or yours?

47:37.104 --> 47:39.898
For some reason,
I feel comfortable being with you today.

47:46.321 --> 47:47.197
It always showed

47:47.948 --> 47:50.701
"anxious" or "uneasy" when I was with you.

47:51.785 --> 47:53.745
See this? It's green.

47:56.248 --> 47:58.917
This means you don't hate me.

47:59.501 --> 48:01.670
My emotions are controlled
by the other person.

48:03.422 --> 48:05.632
If they like me, I'm relieved.

48:06.216 --> 48:08.260
If they don't, I'm anxious.

48:09.970 --> 48:13.140
I'm at the mercy
of other people's emotions

48:13.724 --> 48:14.933
because I soak them up like a sponge.

48:26.737 --> 48:28.238
Knock it off.

48:28.322 --> 48:30.782
It's cramped here. Stay still, will you?

48:32.200 --> 48:33.160
Come on, guys.

48:33.243 --> 48:36.079
-Jeez, get off me! What are you doing?
-Seriously?

48:36.163 --> 48:38.540
-For goodness' sake!
-Are you kidding me?

48:39.541 --> 48:41.001
I'm so sick of these two.

48:51.720 --> 48:52.763
This is nice.

48:57.100 --> 48:58.810
This is great!

49:02.898 --> 49:06.485
We have to be
Zorba the Greek at the beach!

49:06.568 --> 49:07.486
It's been forever!

49:14.701 --> 49:18.497
-Dance, dance, dance, yeah.
-Come on, my boy!

49:21.333 --> 49:23.418
To the left first! Here we go!

49:23.919 --> 49:25.629
-One, two!
-One, two!

49:27.798 --> 49:28.840
Step forward!

49:37.516 --> 49:38.433
Again, step forward!

49:43.188 --> 49:44.106
Let us join!

49:47.025 --> 49:48.026
All right!

49:51.697 --> 49:53.990
-All right!
-Let's go!

50:12.342 --> 50:13.552
What a bunch of morons.

50:30.819 --> 50:33.238
Hey, he figured out the ending.

50:34.364 --> 50:35.991
Yeong-su, that's it!

50:36.742 --> 50:38.493
Don't make any more revisions!

50:47.294 --> 50:49.880
I feel like I'll relive this memory
before I die.

50:53.842 --> 50:55.719
Am I really reminiscing right now?

51:06.354 --> 51:07.564
Let's get going!

51:10.692 --> 51:12.194
I can't read your handwriting.

51:12.277 --> 51:14.988
We should watch the sun rise before we go.

51:15.071 --> 51:17.532
After all, we came all the way
to the East Sea.

51:17.616 --> 51:20.368
-Let's watch it before we go!
-Let's do that!

51:20.452 --> 51:22.454
The sun won't rise for another few hours.

51:22.537 --> 51:25.373
We can just grab coffee
at a convenience store and wait.

51:25.457 --> 51:27.292
Just tell me already!

51:32.047 --> 51:33.757
Who likes who exactly?

51:35.592 --> 51:36.843
This energy doesn't come from stamina.

51:37.594 --> 51:39.721
No one our age has this kind of stamina.

51:40.597 --> 51:45.018
Who goes for second and third rounds,
and ends up at a beach at our age?

51:45.101 --> 51:46.937
Clearly, someone likes someone here,

51:47.020 --> 51:48.688
and I'm the sacrificial lamb.

51:49.564 --> 51:50.607
So tell me who it is.

52:01.076 --> 52:02.619
I like Hwang Dong-man.

52:16.633 --> 52:22.097
I like Hwang Dong-man.

52:22.180 --> 52:23.557
Was that a buzz?

52:23.640 --> 52:26.726
And you like me too…

52:26.810 --> 52:27.978
AWKWARD

52:28.061 --> 52:28.895
Huh?

52:31.314 --> 52:32.482
What do you mean "awkward"?

52:36.278 --> 52:37.487
Tell me!

52:39.739 --> 52:40.824
I like…

52:41.533 --> 52:43.326
Ms. Byeon Eun-a.

52:59.467 --> 53:02.012
If I catch any of you texting each other,
you're dead.

53:05.390 --> 53:07.309
And of course, you just stop instantly.

53:11.396 --> 53:13.315
I mean, seriously? "Awkward"?

53:13.398 --> 53:16.234
Why feel awkward?
Did I ask you to like me back?

53:16.318 --> 53:19.321
Who says we can only like one person?
Why are people so narrow-minded?

53:19.404 --> 53:20.572
Byeon Eun-a.

53:20.655 --> 53:21.865
Is that what you think too?

53:21.948 --> 53:25.535
Is it right for him to feel awkward
because I said I like him?

53:25.619 --> 53:28.079
I'd be thrilled if someone I like
said they liked me.

53:28.163 --> 53:29.164
Wouldn't you?

53:30.832 --> 53:32.834
-I would.
-Exactly!

53:33.543 --> 53:34.961
So how could you feel awkward?

53:36.338 --> 53:38.590
Huh? Hey, mister!

53:38.673 --> 53:39.507
Are you sleeping?

53:40.091 --> 53:43.178
-In a situation like this?
-Yeong-su, wake up.

53:43.261 --> 53:44.179
Wake up.

53:46.306 --> 53:48.433
He hasn't slept these past few days.

53:48.516 --> 53:51.561
How could he sleep when I'm so pissed off?

53:51.645 --> 53:53.396
"Awkward"? Are you kidding me?

53:57.025 --> 53:58.693
What the heck is going on?!

54:00.236 --> 54:02.948
Hit the brakes! The brakes!

54:32.978 --> 54:35.397
My wish is to die of old age.

54:36.189 --> 54:37.440
Not from agony,

54:38.108 --> 54:39.484
not from humiliation.

54:40.610 --> 54:41.778
I want to die of old age.

54:48.410 --> 54:49.494
Go sleep inside.

55:07.262 --> 55:08.263
You know…

55:12.475 --> 55:15.061
I can always tell
whether someone's really asleep

55:16.271 --> 55:17.897
or just pretending.

55:20.150 --> 55:21.901
So why are you pretending to sleep?

55:24.863 --> 55:25.905
Just because.

55:27.699 --> 55:29.200
I'm tired.

56:10.784 --> 56:11.826
Step away.

56:12.619 --> 56:15.538
Step away
from Director Lee Jun-hwan's film.

56:16.164 --> 56:18.583
Production costs
will be at least 20 billion won.

56:19.167 --> 56:21.169
What kind of producer debuts
with a 20 billion won film?

56:21.252 --> 56:24.005
Start with something small
and build up your experience.

56:24.089 --> 56:25.632
You can work on a big one next time.

56:27.008 --> 56:29.010
I'm the one who set this in motion,

56:29.761 --> 56:31.846
and I cast Jang Mi-ran.

56:34.891 --> 56:36.142
Didn't you get a paycheck?

56:36.226 --> 56:37.644
Did you work for free?

56:38.394 --> 56:41.189
If you want a stake in this,
work as a freelancer.

56:41.272 --> 56:42.607
You've got some nerve.

56:42.690 --> 56:43.983
You haven't even produced anything,

56:44.067 --> 56:45.902
and you think you can handle
a 20-billion-won project?

56:45.985 --> 56:47.487
Do you know what investing is?

56:47.570 --> 56:48.905
Have you ever worked with a VC?

56:48.988 --> 56:51.866
Do you know anything about camera models,
budgets, or how many you need?

56:52.450 --> 56:53.535
Of course, you don't.

56:58.957 --> 57:00.500
Was it Ms. Oh Jeong-hui's request

57:02.460 --> 57:03.503
to kick me off the project?

57:08.383 --> 57:10.343
What do you take me for, a lackey?

57:10.426 --> 57:13.429
Do I look like someone who takes orders
and acts on them?

57:13.513 --> 57:17.016
Choi Film is my company,
and it's my money!

57:34.742 --> 57:36.453
Ms. Oh Jeong-hui would like to see you.

57:37.120 --> 57:39.581
I'll be waiting in the car near Choi Film.

58:24.959 --> 58:27.253
You told me not to let anyone find out,

58:28.630 --> 58:31.090
so how does it make any sense
that you're getting close to Mi-ran?

58:32.467 --> 58:35.220
If you decided to change your name
and live as a different person,

58:35.303 --> 58:37.138
you never should've
stepped into this world.

58:37.889 --> 58:39.015
It was Dad's world too.

58:39.641 --> 58:41.601
A place he walked away from
without any respect.

58:42.685 --> 58:45.104
I wondered what the big deal was
with the people here.

58:46.481 --> 58:47.690
Turns out, they're nothing special.

58:48.566 --> 58:50.568
They have nothing but elitist attitudes

58:50.652 --> 58:51.819
and are painfully old-fashioned.

58:57.909 --> 58:59.494
Is that why you're seeing a guy like that?

59:00.537 --> 59:02.163
Out of pity for your dad?

59:03.665 --> 59:05.291
I know why you find him appealing.

59:05.875 --> 59:07.085
He's wild and unruly,

59:08.461 --> 59:10.421
like a half-grown boy.

59:11.005 --> 59:12.590
But he has potential, right?

59:13.299 --> 59:14.884
See for yourself if he really does.

59:15.510 --> 59:18.054
The most dreadful thing in the world
is an incompetent man.

59:18.721 --> 59:21.474
An incompetent man
is nothing more than a castrated male.

59:25.645 --> 59:26.479
So tell me.

59:28.022 --> 59:30.400
Are you satisfied
with your competent husband?

59:32.652 --> 59:34.195
When I look at the streets,

59:35.738 --> 59:37.865
I don't see people walking.

59:37.949 --> 59:40.660
I see masses of emotion walking around.

59:41.244 --> 59:43.538
You can see their complete emotional state

59:44.163 --> 59:46.541
in every step they take
and every expression they make.

59:48.710 --> 59:50.545
That's why I don't see them as people

59:51.546 --> 59:53.089
but as masses of emotion.

59:54.799 --> 59:57.176
Do you know what mass of emotion you are?

01:00:00.096 --> 01:00:01.222
A mass of contempt.

01:00:03.266 --> 01:00:06.561
Have you ever looked at someone
sitting across from you without contempt?

01:00:08.521 --> 01:00:09.939
You find everyone pathetic,

01:00:10.898 --> 01:00:12.317
and you don't like anyone.

01:00:13.318 --> 01:00:15.778
After leaving
your pathetic husband and child,

01:00:16.362 --> 01:00:19.991
you replaced them
with a shiny new husband and child.

01:00:22.577 --> 01:00:24.829
So isn't it about time
you let go of that contempt?

01:00:26.706 --> 01:00:28.916
But I guess something inside you
is still missing.

01:00:49.103 --> 01:00:51.314
NO ONE COMES INTO YOUR LIFE BY MISTAKE

01:00:53.149 --> 01:00:56.986
I contacted an agency to see
if they could look up Byeon Si-on online.

01:00:57.570 --> 01:00:59.364
They found a file from your high school

01:01:00.198 --> 01:01:02.825
that listed your guardian as "Ga Su-ja."

01:01:03.534 --> 01:01:04.786
EMERGENCY CONTACT LIST

01:01:04.869 --> 01:01:07.205
NAME: BYEON SI-ON
GUARDIAN: GA SU-JA

01:01:07.288 --> 01:01:09.707
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

01:01:09.791 --> 01:01:11.834
Thank you. Have a good day.

01:01:17.632 --> 01:01:19.842
It's a unique name, so it'll be easy
for people to track her down.

01:01:20.468 --> 01:01:22.261
The file has been deleted,

01:01:22.345 --> 01:01:23.805
but someone might've seen it already,

01:01:24.305 --> 01:01:26.224
so you should move out of that house.

01:01:31.646 --> 01:01:33.481
This is a brand-new
studio apartment in Gangbuk.

01:01:33.564 --> 01:01:36.234
It's fully furnished,
so you just have to move in.

01:01:39.904 --> 01:01:40.822
And this is a cash card.

01:01:41.322 --> 01:01:43.991
The PIN is the last four digits
of your phone number.

01:01:59.090 --> 01:02:01.175
Let me know
if you don't like living there.

01:02:01.259 --> 01:02:02.343
I'll find another place.

01:02:03.261 --> 01:02:04.512
I'll even buy you one if you want.

01:02:05.638 --> 01:02:08.391
You said you wouldn't let anyone find out

01:02:09.058 --> 01:02:10.768
that you're actually the poor,
little Byeon Si-on.

01:02:11.394 --> 01:02:12.270
So just move out.

01:02:12.854 --> 01:02:14.021
You're embarrassed

01:02:15.314 --> 01:02:16.399
that I live in a place like that

01:02:17.150 --> 01:02:18.192
with my step-grandmother.

01:02:18.276 --> 01:02:20.111
Yeah, it's embarrassing.

01:02:21.070 --> 01:02:23.740
It's embarrassing,
and I'm bound to get criticized.

01:02:24.824 --> 01:02:27.660
No one would care
if you lived with your dad there.

01:02:27.744 --> 01:02:29.954
But it's a different situation
with him gone.

01:02:39.839 --> 01:02:42.008
I wish I had been born
from a bamboo shoot.

01:02:42.925 --> 01:02:44.093
It would've been so nice

01:02:44.594 --> 01:02:46.262
to have been born out of thin air,

01:02:47.555 --> 01:02:49.640
with no need for sperm, eggs,
a mother, or a father.

01:02:56.189 --> 01:02:57.398
Just know this.

01:02:59.150 --> 01:03:01.444
It's not your fault
I didn't turn out better.

01:03:03.070 --> 01:03:05.114
But I'm going to be really successful.

01:03:06.824 --> 01:03:08.826
But when I imagine myself doing well,

01:03:10.077 --> 01:03:12.914
I get pissed off
thinking about you showing up…

01:03:15.291 --> 01:03:16.417
smiling and clinging to me.

01:03:18.878 --> 01:03:21.297
A mother rejecting a child
for not being good enough is one thing.

01:03:22.548 --> 01:03:25.426
But a mother who clings
to a successful one like a leech…

01:03:27.470 --> 01:03:28.596
is even worse.

01:03:33.059 --> 01:03:34.060
So don't ever

01:03:35.728 --> 01:03:36.729
act like…

01:03:38.981 --> 01:03:40.191
we're close.

01:04:33.911 --> 01:04:34.912
Help me.

01:04:37.999 --> 01:04:38.833
MS. BYEON EUN-A

01:04:53.764 --> 01:04:55.683
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable…

01:05:55.618 --> 01:05:57.411
WE ARE ALL TRYING HERE

01:06:15.513 --> 01:06:16.889
This screenplay is insane.

01:06:16.973 --> 01:06:18.224
Keep a room open tonight.

01:06:18.307 --> 01:06:20.267
Noh Kang-sik will be coming.

01:06:20.351 --> 01:06:22.937
Make sure Dong-man stays away
from Agit today.

01:06:23.020 --> 01:06:25.356
Why are you refusing the money
and the house?

01:06:25.439 --> 01:06:28.526
Would it be okay if I registered
my grandma's address at your place?

01:06:28.609 --> 01:06:30.528
-Who's the director again?
-Nice to meet you.

01:06:30.611 --> 01:06:33.489
When someone does well,
I really feel sick to my stomach.

01:06:33.572 --> 01:06:36.158
Don't ruin something
someone poured everything into.

01:06:36.242 --> 01:06:37.201
Let's produce this ourselves.

01:06:37.284 --> 01:06:38.119
We'll take it from here.

01:06:38.202 --> 01:06:39.495
The director said he'd work with me.

01:06:39.578 --> 01:06:40.955
I did it because nobody else can!

01:06:41.038 --> 01:06:44.250
I did it because everyone's afraid
of a piece of trash like him!

01:06:45.251 --> 01:06:49.922
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
